{"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/incidencegraphview"]}],"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An undirected hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Graph"},{"type":"text","text":" on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n + m"},{"type":"text","text":" whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i < n"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" and whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is hyperedge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"type":"text","text":", with an edge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{i, n + p}"},{"type":"text","text":" for each incidence. It is bipartite and simple"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(vertices on the left, hyperedges on the right), an empty hyperedge is an isolated vertex, and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it loses nothing."}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","kind":"relationships"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView"},"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView.swift#L48","fileName":"IncidenceGraphView.swift"},"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceGraphView"}],"externalID":"s:11Hypergraphs18IncidenceGraphViewV","roleHeading":"Structure","title":"IncidenceGraphView","symbolKind":"struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceGraphView"}],"modules":[{"name":"Hypergraphs"}]},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"IncidenceGraphView"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Base"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols10HypergraphP","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hypergraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Edge position ","type":"text"},{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is incidence number ","type":"text"},{"code":"q","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":": the incidences hyperedge by hyperedge, in index","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"order, and within a hyperedge in ","type":"text"},{"code":"memberIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order. So ","type":"text"},{"code":"edges[q]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"UndirectedEdge(i, n + p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the rows of the hyperedge side are contiguous ranges, and a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"per-incidence array (a weight of a vertex in a hyperedge) is indexed by edge position. A view is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a snapshot, so its own positions never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only until","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"its next mutation: the view of the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"IncidenceMatrix","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", inserting one cell shifts every later incidence by one), and a per-incidence","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"array must be rebuilt for it.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every index member reads the base’s rows: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"neighborIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)"},{"type":"text","text":" shifted by n, and of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"memberIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)"},{"type":"text","text":". "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Traversal"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Connectivity"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ShortestPaths"},{"type":"text","text":" and the rest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"therefore run on the view without hashing a vertex. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withIncidentIndexRows"},{"type":"text","text":" writes the view’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"rows out once per call from the base’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_withIncidenceRows"},{"type":"text","text":", in O(n + m + p), for whole-graph"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms (components, bridges, cut vertices)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The view keeps each hyperedge’s first incidence number, so a hyperedge’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"text":" is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range, O(1). On ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"UndirectedIncidenceList"},{"text":", which stores its incidences, every read is O(1) plus","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the row. On any other base, ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"endpointIndices(ofEdgeAt:)"},{"text":" binary-search the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hyperedge and find the member by its rank (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberIndex(atRank:…)"},{"text":"), O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"text":" and O(log m + k) by default, and a vertex’s ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"incidentEdges"},{"text":" finds its place in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"each of its hyperedges: O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceMatrix"},{"text":", which counts bits, and O(Σ k) over","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"them on a base without a faster ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberRank"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BipartiteGraph(h.incidenceGraphView, left: 0 ..< h.vertexCount)"},{"text":" gives the bipartite structure,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and the view’s components restricted to ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n"},{"text":" are the hypergraph’s.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Edges-swift.struct","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/IncidentEdgeIndices","doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/Neighbors"],"generated":true},{"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/IncidenceGraphView\/init(base:)"],"generated":true},{"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Propert